===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
{{suffix|en|behavior|ism}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} {{term-label|en|American spelling}}

# An approach to [[psychology]] focusing on [[observable]] [[behavior]] which, generally assuming that behavior is determined by the [[environment]] and denying any [[independent]] [[significance]] for [[mind]], largely ignores any [[pathophysiological]] processes which may, or may not, underlie subjective, behavioral [[phenomena]].
#: '''''Behaviorism''' is considered by most philosophers of medicine, to be an expression of the minimalist interpretation of the 'medical model' of psychology because it focuses the study and classification of mental [[disorder]]s upon a [[phenomenological]], rather than a [[pathophysiological]], approach to the subject.

